{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1009109-how-to-encourage-set-situations-that-get-mages-to-reach","id":1009109,"title":"How to encourage / set situations that get Mages to reach?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-11-27T18:35:26-08:00","id":1009109,"title":"How to encourage / set situations that get Mages to reach?","content":"After a few games I have noticed that my group doesn't feel the need / willing to Reach beyond their grasp or risk Paradox in virtually any way?<br /> <br /> It feels like, without Paradox, we are missing out on a lot of interesting and colorful aspects of magic.<br /> <br /> So what are some ideas that would encourage the players to risk paradox?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4011-weaverchilde","name":"Weaverchilde","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-27T18:44:30-08:00","id":1009114,"title":"","content":"Generally speaking, you won't have to try for starting Mages. Any situation that is dangerous enough is one that will make them Reach.<br /> <br /> If you want to create a situation where a character Reaches beyond their natural range, though, look at their arcana, find a Practice used by the top dot they have in it, and make it crucial to use in a way that is big and impressive somehow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-27T19:09:14-08:00","id":1009127,"title":"","content":"It seems like what you really want is a greater risk of Paradox. Reaching is just one way to accomplish that. It's pretty easy to set up a situation where they're going to need more than their safe limit in spells in order to accomplish a task, especially at low levels of Gnosis. At higher levels of Gnosis going over your safe Reach even a little bit induces a much higher risk of Paradox. If they risk Paradox in any way it's possible to keep them from buying the Paradox dice pool down too much by placing a time crunch on their spellcasting which limits how quickly they can spend mana to mitigate.<br /> <br /> If your players are using creative thaumaturgy a lot (And by that I mean making up spells that don't exist in the book) it's best to construct the spells so they accomplish something very basic and refinements in application and power cost Reach. It's also possible to add Reach clauses to existing spells for instance one of my players used Gravity Supremacy and I let him apply the Immobilized Tilt by spending a Reach which put him over the safe Reach limit.<br /> <br /> You can also put them in situations where Sleeper witnesses will see them doing obvious magic, or places where Abyssal interaction is more likely.<br /> <br /> In the end though, if your players aren't risking Paradox then don't sweat it. The game isn't about inducing Paradox, and frankly I'm not sure that's where you should be getting your jollies. Games are for running awesome stories, a Paradox can be a nice twist, but it's not the point of the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-27T20:01:33-08:00","id":1009138,"title":"","content":"See my group is the sort that will turn the air around the rampaging Vampire solid (and as strong as steel) and then kill him while immobilized... which is surprisingly easy to do with Matter 3 and it feel a bit dickish to target their weak spots just to make a challenge. (which I could easily do since no one in the group has time or fate)<br /> <br /> Well, its not about getting &quot;Jollies&quot;. I have been running Apocalypse World for the last couple years as a series of one shots and the thing I love about that mechanic is that when the character fails, there is something interesting and unforeseen that happens to move the story forward (something I was not planning for) and that is how I see paradox. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4011-weaverchilde","name":"Weaverchilde","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-27T20:44:43-08:00","id":1009148,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weaverchilde</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1009109-how-to-encourage-set-situations-that-get-mages-to-reach?p=1009138#post1009138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See my group is the sort that will turn the air around the rampaging Vampire solid (and as strong as steel) and then kill him while immobilized... which is surprisingly easy to do with Matter 3 and it feel a bit dickish to target their weak spots just to make a challenge.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is a rote form of State Change the culprit for this particular example or are we talking about a cabal of Adepts?<br /> <br /> Because between instant casting and transmuting a gas directly into a solid, they pretty much have to choose between Sensory Range and Advanced Duration for their third free Reach, to say nothing of how &quot;strong as steel&quot; is going to require a -4 penalty for the Durability alone \u2014 otherwise that rampaging vampire is going to break their solid-air straightjacket about as easily as a piece of cheap window glass.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T01:52:45-08:00","id":1009238,"title":"","content":"If you're only giving a group of Mages one obvious target at a time they will wipe the floor with it. It's true that Mages are at their most impressive with time to prepare, but they can still manage to do an awful lot very quickly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T01:56:34-08:00","id":1009239,"title":"","content":"Keep the pressure on them. Provide multiple things they have to accomplish <i>right now</i>. The Mysteries do not form an orderly queue.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T07:32:10-08:00","id":1009322,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1009109-how-to-encourage-set-situations-that-get-mages-to-reach?p=1009148#post1009148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is a rote form of State Change the culprit for this particular example or are we talking about a cabal of Adepts?<br /> <br /> Because between instant casting and transmuting a gas directly into a solid, they pretty much have to choose between Sensory Range and Advanced Duration for their third free Reach, to say nothing of how &quot;strong as steel&quot; is going to require a -4 penalty for the Durability alone \u2014 otherwise that rampaging vampire is going to break their solid-air straightjacket about as easily as a piece of cheap window glass.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is a Rote, with a set of 4 starting stat characters. <br /> <br /> And this here is the post that my player made:<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1001342-a-couple-queries-concerning-namely-matter\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1001342-a-couple-queries-concerning-namely-matter\"> A couple queries concerning namely Matter - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1001342-a-couple-queries-concerning-namely-matter\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1001342-a-couple-queries-concerning-namely-matter </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> I'm looking for some additional opinions as to what some of the board might think regarding a few matter effects/spells. A couple of these have come up during some </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Matter has been... interesting in our games with State Change and Wonderful Machine<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1009109-how-to-encourage-set-situations-that-get-mages-to-reach?p=1009239#post1009239\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Keep the pressure on them. Provide multiple things they have to accomplish <i>right now</i>. The Mysteries do not form an orderly queue.</div> </div> </div> </div>So I do this like the Cake song &quot;The Distance&quot; - Assail him, impale him with monster-truck force. <br /> <br /> It may also be prudent to have the Mysteries push on them instead of just letting them poke at them","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4011-weaverchilde","name":"Weaverchilde","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T07:54:31-08:00","id":1009332,"title":"","content":"Pretty much, it doesn't have to be a direct threat either. My players were just meeting a couple of Sleepers from their mortal lives and stumbled into a small group of monsters in Mind Twilight ripping something out of Sleepers in the area. They managed to capture three. Capturing those forced going over on Reach pretty quickly because they only reacted to monsters appearing one by one instead of looking for more, and it was happening too fast to mitigate Paradox. They were smart and contained Paradox effectively, but I was up to 6 Paradox dice by the third one. They couldn't handle the rest and protect their Sleeper friends simultaneously. Obviously they're not going to be able to just let these things run amok either. I expect they'll handle it better upon returning.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 11-28-2016, 10:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T02:46:45-08:00","id":1010121,"title":"","content":"What would you do if they decided that these monsters deserve it and are not worth the effort of being protected from Paradox? Imagine that they decide to release the Paradox instead of containing it (I assume the spells in questions targeted the Mind Monsters, so Paradox would claw at them).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T03:37:06-08:00","id":1010136,"title":"","content":"Depends on the spell and what I think would have been interesting at the time. I only ever rolled one success for the Dox per spell though so it would have been a Havoc. Probably I'd switch the target of the spell from one of the monsters to one of their victim Sleepers. I'm not sure what I'll do when they go back, but I kind of expect there to be less Dox anyway if it comes up at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T04:03:11-08:00","id":1010140,"title":"","content":"Mmm. That's two successes result. <br /> To the op:<br /> One of was to encourage people to Reach is making Releasing Paradox a tempting deal; it penalizes your spellcasting, but Paradox Condition is applied to the subject, not you. If you want to make Reaching more exciting, try to make released Paradoxes less...antagonistic. If people will perceive it as &quot;we are handling our GM a rope to hang us with&quot;, they won't reach too much, and when they will, they will try to contain at all costs. Try to make released Paradox terrible and terryfing...but not always antagonistic. In the Mind Demons example, if a player would release Paradox thinking &quot;they don't deserve being saved from this dox&quot;, bestow a negative Condition on the poor demon. <br /> <br /> Paradox *can* help players. By making it as much as potential ally as a threat, you make paradoxing tempting and cool. Making all side-effects negative will make people just avoid it as a pain in the ass and direct danger to themselves (this includes all of the &quot;dickish&quot; options - ricochet, un-making Reaches). <br /> Again, one of more interesting aspects of Wisdom is asking yourself the question what side effects of releasing are acceptable and which ones aren't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T04:32:05-08:00","id":1010148,"title":"","content":"You're right, switching targets take two Reach so I'd have probably go with Advanced Scale then and hit all the Sleepers and monsters in the area in one go. Which would have been more efficient but have possibly serious consequences for the Integrity of affected Sleepers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T05:50:33-08:00","id":1010163,"title":"","content":"That's cool! As a rule, I try to make released Paradox relatively safe or even beneficial for the caster (I assume that if they managed to cast the spell through the dice penalty bestowed by Paradox, there is no need to kick them more); side effects like this are the best, because they don't necessarily undo the spell, and might be a net gain overall, but...they also challenge your Wisdom. And of course, many player characters will try to help these poor Sleepers. For the first, second, and tenth time...question is, what about 30rd and 80th time it happens? It's very easy to just be all like &quot;meh, can't bother&quot;. <br /> <br /> Of course, this isn't the only way to handle Paradox. But it certainly can help to encourage certain groups, especially those that avoid anything that harm their characters directly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T06:15:05-08:00","id":1010169,"title":"","content":"Their Wisdom is at risk as well so I doubt they could just ignore the consequences forever. One thing I definitely decided to do is every time a Paradox does happen it spreads their Long Term Nimbus effects to their Sympathetic ties. My players are new and their characters are young so for now it'll be subtle, but it will get more obvious that carelessness leads back to hurting the ones you care about even if it doesn't touch you directly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}